                    },
                    "message": "This increases the call to sd_bus for message unpacking of multiple args."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Yep, will characterize performance impact and rework if needed."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Didn't mean to resolve."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I was only able to find 2 instances of interfaces that could use the group optimization.\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/ipmbbridge/blob/35e1485f76a1562d0782a3a0dc003d0a7ac76ed9/ipmbbridged.cpp#L854\n\nAnd ipmi\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/phosphor-host-ipmid/blob/920602f5f89b7aeeb7fd31dc77c768f1149cc1f2/ipmid-new.cpp#L493\n\nI wasn't able to see any meaningful performance change in either under-load CPU usage (running ipmitool sensor list in a fast loop) with this patch for ipmi.\n\n\n\nI think the overall improvement in compile times isn't worth having the hypothetical improvement by grouping systemd calls for what amounts to 2 APIs.\n\n\nPlease reconsider this and let me know your thoughts."
                }
            ],
